---
import Slide from '../ui/Slide.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../ui/CodeBlock.astro';
import Callout from '../ui/Callout.astro';
---

<Slide
  id="s39c-endpointslices"
  chapter="Failure Patterns"
  title="EndpointSlices — Ready Backends Proof"
  track="core"
  notes="Modern clusters use EndpointSlices; Endpoints may still exist as compatibility. Empty slices = no Ready backends. Always check both when traffic dies."
>
  <div class="stagger flex flex-col gap-6">
    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-deck-border bg-deck-panel p-5">
        <div class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-deck-cyan">Endpoints</div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-lg text-deck-muted">Legacy aggregate view of ready pod IPs.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-deck-border bg-deck-panel p-5">
        <div class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-deck-amber">EndpointSlice</div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-lg text-deck-muted">Scalable, partitioned ready backends — what kube-proxy often consumes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <CodeBlock
      caption="Service exists but no traffic"
      code={`kubectl get endpoints SERVICE -n NS -o wide
kubectl get endpointslices -n NS -l kubernetes.io/service-name=SERVICE -o wide
# Empty addresses / conditions → selector or readiness problem`}
    />

    <Callout type="rule">
      Selector mismatch and Not Ready pods both produce empty EndpointSlices. Fix labels/probes before blaming CNI.
    </Callout>
  </div>
</Slide>
